{
 "spec_version": "future_lab.monitoring.v1",
 "frozen_on": "2026-09-23",
 "status": "PROPOSED. It becomes pre-specified only once its sha256 is registered in research/preregistrations.jsonl before each candidate's forward_start. Parameters must not be re-estimated on forward data.",
 "not_evidence": "Priors, SE inflation and drawdown boundaries are estimated from already-observed history. The rule tests whether forward data is consistent with that history; it cannot anticipate regimes absent from it.",
 "evaluator": "research.future_lab.forward.evaluate_from_spec('reports/future_lab/monitoring_rule_spec.json', name, daily_df) (verifies this sha256, then applies the rule mechanically)",
 "inputs": {
  "daily_df_columns": {
   "ret": "candidate daily net total return",
   "rf": "daily T-bill return",
   "control_ret": "control daily net total return (omit for spy)"
  }
 },
 "rule": {
  "look_every_trading_days": 21,
  "max_months": 60,
  "kill_sharpe": {
   "threshold": 0.3,
   "prob_below": 0.1,
   "min_months": 6
  },
  "kill_drawdown": {
   "percentile": 0.99
  },
  "revert_to_control": {
   "threshold": 0.0,
   "prob_below": 0.1,
   "min_months": 24
  },
  "promote": {
   "min_months": 24,
   "p_sharpe_gt_0": 0.95,
   "p_ir_gt_0": 0.9
  }
 },
 "rule_text": [
  "Looks: at each calendar month-end close, once >= 21 forward trading days exist. months_elapsed = round(trading_days / 21).",
  "Statistics: annualised Sharpe of daily excess returns (ret - rf) since forward_start; annualised IR of daily active returns (ret - control_ret); running max drawdown of the candidate NAV since forward_start.",
  "Posterior: Normal prior N(m, s^2) on the true annualised Sharpe (or IR); the forward estimate is treated as N(true, k^2 / years). posterior precision = 1/s^2 + years/k^2; posterior mean = (m/s^2 + estimate*years/k^2) / precision.",
  "Futility prior (kill / revert): m = prior_sharpe_mean (= 0.5 x backtest Sharpe), s = prior_sharpe_sd (= resampled SE of the backtest Sharpe); likewise prior_ir_mean / prior_ir_sd for the IR.",
  "Promotion prior (sceptical): m = 0, s = skeptical_sharpe_sd (= backtest Sharpe / 1.645) and skeptical_ir_sd; only forward data can carry a promotion.",
  "KILL_DRAWDOWN (checked first, any look): running max drawdown deeper than dd_boundary[months_elapsed-1].",
  "KILL_SHARPE (months_elapsed >= 6): futility-prior posterior P(Sharpe > 0.30) < 0.10.",
  "REVERT_TO_CONTROL (months_elapsed >= 24): futility-prior posterior P(IR vs control > 0) < 0.10 -> hold the control instead.",
  "PROMOTE (months_elapsed >= 24): sceptical-prior posterior P(Sharpe > 0) >= 0.95 AND sceptical-prior posterior P(IR > 0) >= 0.90 AND no open implementation REVIEW. Promotion means eligibility for sizing beyond paper/small size, not certainty.",
  "Decisions are terminal. At 60 months with no decision: END_NO_DECISION (the candidate stays a benchmark)."
 ],
